 ```
 
+#### Max Consecutive Losses
+
+`MaxConsecutiveLosses` looks at the most recent trades within `lookback_period` in minutes (or in candles when using `lookback_period_candles`), and counts how many of them, taken from the most recent backwards, lost money in a row (a trade with profit >= `required_profit` breaks the streak).
+If that streak reaches `trade_limit` or more, trading will stop for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`).
+
+Unlike `StoplossGuard` and `LowProfitPairs`, which look at the total number/profit of trades within the lookback window, `MaxConsecutiveLosses` specifically tracks an uninterrupted losing streak - a single winning trade resets the counter.
+
+This applies across all pairs, unless `only_per_pair` is set to true, which will then only look at one pair at a time.
+
+Similarly, this protection will by default look at all trades (long and short). For futures bots, setting `only_per_side` will make the bot only consider one side, and will then only lock this one side.
+
+The below example stops trading a pair for 12 candles after 4 losing trades occurred in a row (within the last 24 candles).
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxConsecutiveLosses",
+            "lookback_period_candles": 24,
+            "trade_limit": 4,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 12,
+            "required_profit": 0.0,
+            "only_per_pair": False,
+            "only_per_side": False
+        }
+    ]
+```
+
+!!! Note
+    Set `only_per_pair: False` (the default) to also stop the bot globally once losses pile up in a row across all pairs, not just for one specific pair.
+
 #### Cooldown Period
 
 `CooldownPeriod` locks a pair for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`) after exiting, avoiding a re-entry for this pair for `stop_duration` minutes.
